From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-controller: clean node respect shared identity
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

Do not let an aged-out duplicate delete the identity of its live twin.

cntlr_clean_node() removes the mac_table ALID entry, the UCI node and radio
sections and the topology device purely by AL-MAC. All of those are shared
with any duplicate node object carrying the same AL-MAC, and mac_table holds
exactly one entry per AL-MAC - pointing at whichever object got there first.

So aging out a duplicate deletes the surviving twin identity: the twin can no
longer be found by cntlr_find_node(), stops being refreshed by incoming CMDUs
and expires 65 s later. Observed in the lab as "node ages out and never comes
back" across three consecutive induced-flap cycles.

Perform the AL-MAC-keyed deletions only from the object the mac_table actually
points at. Per-object cleanup (stalist, radiolist, apmld) is unconditional.

The warn() marks a state that should not exist at all once node identity is
single-sourced; it is a diagnostic, not an expected path.

--- a/src/cntlr.c
+++ b/src/cntlr.c
@@ -1655,14 +1655,33 @@
 	if (!timestamp_expired(&n->last_tsp_seen, NODE_EXPIRE_TIME * 1000))
 		return false;
 
-	list_for_each_entry_safe(r, temp, &n->radiolist, list)
-		cntlr_config_del_radio(n->almacaddr);
+	/* Everything keyed purely by AL-MAC (mac_table entry, UCI node/radio
+	 * sections, topology device) is SHARED with any duplicate node object
+	 * carrying the same AL-MAC. mac_table holds exactly one entry per
+	 * AL-MAC, so aging out a duplicate would otherwise delete the identity
+	 * of its still-live twin: the twin stops being findable, stops being
+	 * refreshed, and expires 65 s later. Only the object the mac_table
+	 * actually points at may perform those deletions. */
+	{
+		struct macaddr_entry *_e =
+			mactable_lookup(c->mac_table, n->almacaddr, MAC_ENTRY_ALID);
+		bool owns_identity = (_e && _e->data == (void *)n);
+
+		if (owns_identity) {
+			list_for_each_entry_safe(r, temp, &n->radiolist, list)
+				cntlr_config_del_radio(n->almacaddr);
+
+			cntlr_config_del_node(n->almacaddr);
+			topology_remove_device(&c->topology, n->almacaddr);
+			mactable_del_entry(c->mac_table, n->almacaddr, MAC_ENTRY_ALID);
+		} else {
+			warn("%s: aging out duplicate node " MACFMT " - keeping shared identity for live twin\n",
+			     __func__, MAC2STR(n->almacaddr));
+		}
+	}
 
-	cntlr_config_del_node(n->almacaddr);
-	topology_remove_device(&c->topology, n->almacaddr);
 	node_clean_stalist(c, n);
 	cntlr_clean_radiolist(c, n);
-	mactable_del_entry(c->mac_table, n->almacaddr, MAC_ENTRY_ALID);
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
 	cntlr_free_apmld_list(n);
 #endif
